// Firebase Realtime Database stores JSON data in a JSON Tree structure

### Push new JSON data to the path
POST https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Create Assignment 1 project",
  "priority": "High",
  "done": false
}

### Read JSON data by path
GET https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task.json

### Read JSON data by path and primary key value
@primaryKeyValue = -OkZWeu_RRTOd9yPXs4H
GET https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json

### Write JSON data - will replace all properties with the properties in the request body - if you miss a property it will be removed
PUT https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Commit and push Assignment 1",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "done": true
}

### Remove JSON data - use this if you want to delete data
@deletePrimaryKeyValue = -OkUZJxnTZ4uPU08QbRk
DELETE https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task/{{deletePrimaryKeyValue}}.json

### Update data - use this if you want to update some of the properties but not all of them
PATCH https://dmit2015-1251-a01-swu-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "propertyName": "propertyValue"
}